{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Measured: the existing fix-unit grouping (citric-alert-dogfish, 5e64) has never fired\n\nMain already carries a cross-criterion grouping step for BLOCKING findings: `_group_blocking_fix_units` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/floors.py`, keyed by `sidecar.fix_unit_key` = sha256(token-set(location) + \"|\" + token-set(finding text)), criteria-free, stamp-only (`group_id`, `is_primary`, `group_criteria`; every member keeps `decision=block`; only the CLI renderer collapses). The discovery-stage `review_kernel.suppress_and_dedup` (bug 5e40 B2) is criterion-scoped by its documented key and does not apply here.\n\nThe key requires the two findings' significant-token SETS to be identical for both location and text. Independent finder calls reword both, so it never matches:\n\n- All 9,756 local `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars: 5,838 persist the `group_id` field; **0** carry a stamp; **0** have two blocking findings sharing a `fix_unit_key` on recompute.\n- carbon Group A (the 3 blocking members E4/G1G2/T1): 3 distinct keys; pairwise text token Jaccard 0.33-0.48, location 0.27-0.46. The T3 member is advisory, which 5e64 scoped out of grouping.\n- Bakeoff join (31 adjudicated runs with a matching verdict; the join recovered 16 judged-duplicate pairs from 3 runs, fewer than the 24 groups in the comment above): `fix_unit_key` equal on **0/16**.\n\nNo lexical rule tried separates duplicates cleanly on blocking pairs (10 duplicate, 84 non-duplicate): text Jaccard >= 0.35 catches 2/10 with 0 false merges; shared cited path + text Jaccard >= 0.15 catches 5/10 with 6/84 false merges. Choosing a detection rule is a design decision; no code changed."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793501497724815001,"uuid":"d35fac5c-01b2-476c-a6c2-b7aef976e193"}